# React Native Accessibility Rules

- Support VoiceOver and TalkBack on critical journeys.
- Controls expose role, label, and state where needed.
- Icon-only controls need accessible labels.
- Minimum touch target is 44x44 points; use hitSlop for compact controls.
- Respect dynamic type and reduced motion.
- Never use color alone for state.
- Inputs have visible labels or clear accessibility labels.
- RNTL and Maestro tests assert important roles/labels.
